# WorldSim v5 environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE CODE AUTH — pick ONE of the three methods below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code runs INSIDE a Modal sandbox (see worldsim/modal_sandbox.py).
# Credentials are forwarded from your local shell into the sandbox via
# modal.Secret.from_dict. Three auth paths, in priority order:
#
# 1) CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — Claude Pro / Max subscription auth (preferred).
#    Cheapest per sandbox run. If set, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
#    are NOT forwarded — OAuth doesn't route through a proxy.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your_oauth_token_here
#
# 2) ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN + ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL — OpenRouter (or any proxy).
#    Per https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/coding-agents/claude-code-integration:
#    put your OpenRouter key in ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (not ANTHROPIC_API_KEY),
#    set the base URL to https://openrouter.ai/api (no /v1 suffix), and leave
#    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty. The sandbox handles blanking ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#    automatically when ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is set.
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-or-v1-...
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
#
# 3) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY alone — direct Anthropic API, billed per token.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
#
# If CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is set alongside ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OAuth wins.
# Claude Code's internal precedence puts API keys above OAuth, so forwarding
# both would silently bill API credits instead of your subscription.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL AUTHENTICATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How YOU authenticate against Modal to create sandboxes. Easiest path:
# `modal token new` — writes ~/.modal.toml. For CI/containers, set these:
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=ak-...
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=as-...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL NAMED-SECRET OVERRIDE (opt-in, CI-friendly)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you have a curated Modal secret in a shared workspace, set its name
# here and worldsim will use Secret.from_name(<value>) instead of packaging
# your local shell env vars. The OAuth-wins fixup above does NOT apply in
# this mode — whatever env vars the named secret contains are injected
# as-is, so managing them is your responsibility.
#
# Create one with e.g.:
#   modal secret create my-claude-secret CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=claude-...
#
# Then:
# WORLDSIM_CLAUDE_MODAL_SECRET=my-claude-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER USE — evaluation agent LLM (Phases 3 and 4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser Use runs LOCALLY (not in Modal). Its LLM provider is configured
# via the `llm` param in BrowserUseAgent (see worldsim/main.py).
# These keys are LOCAL-ONLY — NOT forwarded into Modal sandboxes.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBARENA BENCHMARK INSTANCES (Phases 3 and 4)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The user stands up WebArena instances per the v5 spec "Prerequisites" section
# and supplies them to the orchestrator via worldsim/main.py configuration.
# These placeholders are just a convenience for editing main.py.
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_URL=http://localhost:7770
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_DB=mysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/opencart
# WORLDSIM_WEBARENA_SHOPPING_RESET=http://localhost:7770/reset

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override where pipeline state and artifacts are written (default: ./logs/).
# WORLDSIM_STATE_DIR=logs
